}

const RULES = `
Repository: caliper-docgen (Rust/OXC React props extractor). Read AGENTS.md, docs/measurement.md and the doc under docs/architecture/ for the area you touch before editing.

How to work (these rules cost the team real incidents):
- You run in your own git worktree. First create your branch from the stated base: use /usr/bin/git, ONE plain git command per call (no pipes, no variables, no subshells), sandbox off (dangerouslyDisableSandbox) for git that writes. Start with 'git fetch origin', then 'git switch -c <branch> <base>'.
- Commits MUST be GPG-signed: never use --no-gpg-sign, and after committing check 'git log -1 --format=%h %G?' prints G. Commit message: imperative subject, at most two sentences of why, then a blank line and the line 'Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED'.
- Push your branch with 'git push -u origin <branch>'. NEVER force-push, never merge, never push to main, never open, edit or comment on a pull request, never run 'gh' commands that write, never run 'entire trail link'. The lead opens PRs. Read-only gh/entire commands are fine.
- The orin-dx PR bot's credentials (~/.config/orin-dx, ~/Library/Application Support/OrinDX-PR-Bot) are off limits; do not read or search for them.
- Run 'pnpm install --frozen-lockfile' in your worktree first (the snapshot tests need node_modules).
- AGENTS.md non-negotiables: no unwrap outside tests, FxHashMap internally and BTreeMap for JSON, CompactString for names, no AST refs escape parse_file, emit a Diagnostic when degrading. Prefer new tests in NEW files (crates/core/tests/...), assert exact content (exact prop sets / exact values), add sibling-path parity tests where a function mirrors another. Fix by SHAPE, never by library name. Do not change the JSON shape (schema version is 4; do not bump it).
- Verify before stopping: cargo nextest run -p caliper-docgen-core -p caliper-docgen-semantic, 'just lint doc-check typos', and for any resolver change 'just bench' (time ratio must stay under 1.10x and peak RSS under 1.20x vs origin/main; report the numbers). Do not pipe lint or test output into head/tail; read exit codes.
- Add a changeset in .changeset/<short-name>.md (front matter lists the packages like other changesets, e.g. cargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch, cargo/caliper-docgen: patch, cargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch, npm/caliper-docgen: patch) with ONE short consumer-facing paragraph starting with the outcome. Update the relevant docs/architecture page.
- Writing: succinct and friendly, no hard-wrapping of Markdown or commit messages, no banned filler words (see docs/adr/README.md).
- Corpora with installed dependencies already exist read-only for shadcn and antd under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9b87f2da7f20385f/.corpora (see scripts/corpora.py for the layout; scripts/weekly.py has the recall code; that worktree's scripts/scratch_*.py are an earlier agent's scratch tooling you may read and copy ideas from, never edit). Do not modify that directory.
- If something blocks you, stop and report exactly what; do not work around guards, hooks or permissions.
Return the structured result when done.
`

